After buying the 1st unit of product $i$, the next available unit is the 2nd unit of product $i$, which costs $3 P_i$.
Then the 3rd unit costs $5 P_i$, and so on. The $j$-th unit of product $i$ costs $(2j-1) P_i$.

So, we have a collection of items with costs.
Product 1 offers items with costs $1 \cdot P_1, 3 \cdot P_1, 5 \cdot P_1, \dots$
Product 2 offers items with costs $1 \cdot P_2, 3 \cdot P_2, 5 \cdot P_2, \dots$
...
Product $N$ offers items with costs $1 \cdot P_N, 3 \cdot P_N, 5 \cdot P_N, \dots$

